SUMMARY:🎃🍂 Halloween Day: The Fall Colours of High Park & Ghost Stor
 ies 👻
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🎃🍂 Halloween Day: The Fall
  Colours of High Park & Ghost Stories 👻\n\n### Fall Colours\, Spooky St
 ories & A Little Halloween Fun\n\nIt's Halloween — so why should the gho
 sts get to have all the fun at night?\n\nJoin us for a **Halloween Day wal
 k through High Park**\, where we'll enjoy the fall colours while stopping 
 along the way for some of the park's stranger\, spookier\, and downright w
 eird stories.\nHigh Park has a long history of ghost stories and local leg
 ends.\n\nFrom stories connected to the **War of 1812** — yes\, *that* Wa
 r of 1812 — to tales of mysterious deaths and people who may not have co
 mpletely left the park behind\, there's plenty of history to make an ordin
 ary fall walk a little more interesting.\nBut don't worry.\n\n**This isn't
  a terrifying ghost hunt.**\n\nIt's Halloween in the middle of the day. 
 👻☀️\nThink **fall colours\, creepy stories\, a few laughs\, and jus
 t enough spooky atmosphere to make you look over your shoulder once or twi
 ce.**\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](h
 ttps://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 What 
 We'll Do\n\nWe'll walk through **High Park**\, stopping at different locat
 ions along the way while I share stories connected to the park's history a
 nd ghostly legends.\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Enjoy the fall colours 🍂
 \n* Explore some of High Park's most interesting locations\n* Hear stories
  of ghosts\, legends\, and strange events 👻\n* Learn a little about the
  park's history\n* Take photos and enjoy the scenery 📸\n* Have some Hal
 loween fun along the way 🎃\n\nWe'll keep a steady walking pace\, with r
 egular stops for storytelling.\nThe walk will remain **outside throughout*
 * — there is no entry into buildings.\n\n***\n\n## 🎃 Halloween Day 
 — So Let's Have Some Fun\n\nThis isn't meant to be a serious paranormal 
 investigation.\nIt's a **Halloween walk**.\n\nSome stories are creepy. Som
 e are strange. Some might make you wonder whether there's actually somethi
 ng going on.\nAnd some are just a good excuse to tell a spooky story while
  walking through the fall leaves.\n\n**You don't have to believe in ghosts
 .**\nYou just have to enjoy a good story.\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall Weather &
  Expectations\n\nThis is an outdoor walk\, so please dress appropriately f
 or the weather.\nHigh Park can be cool and damp in late October\, so bring
  a warm jacket and wear comfortable walking shoes.\nWe'll be walking at a 
 steady pace\, with stops along the way for stories and photos.\n\n***\n\n#
 # 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** High Park sign on the w
 est side at Bloor Street West & High Park Avenue\n🫎 **Look for me in my
  Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **11:00 AM sharp**\nI will only wait *
 *5 minutes.**\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🚶 **Pace:** Stea
 dy walking pace\n🏁 **End Point:** Back where we started\n\n***\n\n## 
 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$10 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewm
 aclean@hotmail.com**\nThis is a **curated\, guided storytelling experience
 **\, rather than one of our regular group walks. The route\, stories\, and
  history have been researched and developed specifically for this experien
 ce.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walkin
 g shoes\n🧥 Warm fall jacket or layers\n📸 Camera or phone\n🎃 Hallo
 ween spirit\nAnd if you want to wear a costume...\n**I'm certainly not goi
 ng to stop you.** 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis is great
  for:\n\n* People who love Halloween 🎃\n* Anyone who enjoys ghost stori
 es\n* Fall-colour enthusiasts 🍂\n* History buffs\n* People looking for 
 something different to do on Halloween Day\n* Anyone who enjoys a good sto
 ry and a few laughs\n* People who want to meet new people while exploring 
 Toronto\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day
  if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events
  may need to be cancelled or changed\, so please keep an eye on the event 
 page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the ev
 ent wall or email **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for th
 e fall colours.** 🍂\n**Stay for the ghost stories.** 👻\n**Leave with
  a new connection — if the ghosts don't get you first.** 🎃
